{"title":"Omega ring","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The omega ring is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ring\" title=\"Ring\">ring</a> containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/b/89b1eff0f3fbfadff3a70567be70a97ab2d25b65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega,-\\omega,1,-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"15\" />. It has the interesting property that whenever one item in the ring is taken to any power, another item in the ring is the result.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Omega_ring&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018003013\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.006 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.011 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 10/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 271/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 189/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.845      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.845      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5644:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018003013 and revision id 27879. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}